* Opamp noninverting golden ngspice reference (VCCS twin of .model OA(AOL=200000 ROUT=1))
* Correct polarity: G element I(n+ -> n-) = gm*V(nc+,nc-), so
* `G1 out 0 vminus in 200000` injects Gm*(V(in) - V(vminus)) INTO out (V+ = in).
* This deck is the polarity fix demanded by review-round-2 H1: the historical
* inverting deck hand-encoded the same flipped G element as the melange bug,
* and no noninverting reference deck existed at all.
.OPTIONS INTERP reltol=1e-4
VMLG in_mlg 0 PWL({PWL})
RMLG in_mlg in 1
R1 0 vminus 1k
R2 vminus out 10k
G1 out 0 vminus in 200000
Rout out 0 1
{TRAN}
.control
run
wrdata {DAT} v(out)
.endc
.END
